### Environment Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 1. User Signup - Create First User (Aditi)
# @name signupUser1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "aditi",
  "email": "aditi@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### 2. User Signup - Create Second User (Rohan)
# @name signupUser2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "rohan",
  "email": "rohan@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### 3. User Login (Aditi)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "aditi@example.com",
  "password": "Password123"
}

### 4. Get Current Profile (Protected with Token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 5. Access Notes Without Token (Expect 403 Forbidden)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notes

### 6. Create Note 1 (Aditi)
# @name createNote1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Backend Architecture Plan",
  "content": "Implement JWT authentication, manual cookie parser, and socket.io chat."
}

### 7. Create Note 2 (Aditi)
# @name createNote2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Database Schema Review",
  "content": "Verify User, Note, and Message models in MongoDB."
}

### 8. Get All Notes for Current User (Expect 200 with 2 notes)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 9. Get Single Note by ID (Replace with created note ID)
@noteId = {{createNote1.response.body._id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 10. Update Note by ID (Owner Only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/notes/{{noteId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Backend Architecture Plan (Updated)",
  "content": "Completed JWT and Socket.io integration. Ready for deployment."
}

### 11. Delete Note by ID (Owner Only)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/notes/{{noteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 12. User Logout (Clears httpOnly cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 13. Admin Endpoint - List All Users (Requires admin role)
# Note: Run `node scripts/makeAdmin.js aditi@example.com` before testing this endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
